15	// `facts proposals` is the user-facing surface for the CROSS-MEMBER review queue: the
16	// conflicts another member's `facts sync` kept both sides of and routed for a human to
17	// settle. It is the hosted twin of `facts review` (which resolves this member's own
18	// low-confidence, on-disk proposals) and shares its verbs: list, show, apply, reject.
19	//
20	// Hosted egress is opt-in and off by default, exactly like `publish` (ADR-P1-A, no
21	// implicit egress): a network call happens only when the user explicitly runs one
22	// of these commands with a target — the connected binding by default, else
23	// explicit flags (COR-2143). The master kill switch (ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS)
24	// always wins. Every gate is checked BEFORE any HTTP request, so a refusal is
25	// guaranteed egress-free and the default behaviour stays strictly local.
26	
27	// factsProposalsOptions bundles the flag state shared by every `facts proposals` verb.
28	type factsProposalsOptions struct {
29		branch  string
30		repoID  string
31		apiURL  string
32		token   string
33		jsonOut bool
34	}
