55			Short: "Review the hosted cross-member conflict queue (opt-in)",
56			Long: `proposals lists and settles the OPEN cross-member review proposals on the
57	hosted fact-set: contradictions two members' facts raised, kept both-sides by the
58	keep-both merge and routed to a human rather than silently overwritten.
59	
60	Accepting a proposal applies its merge/supersede (the losing fact is retained as
61	superseded, never deleted); rejecting it keeps both facts active and clears the
62	conflict cross-link. Either way the resolved fact set and the shrunken open set are
63	pushed under compare-and-swap, so every member converges.
64	
65	This surface is HOSTED and opt-in: nothing leaves your machine unless you run
66	one of these commands with a target — the connected binding by default, or an
67	explicit one. Use ` + "`memories review`" + ` for this member's own local, low-confidence
68	proposals — that path is fully offline.
69	
70	The target resolves flag > env > connected binding: --repo-id /` + " " + envRepoID + `,
71	--api-url / ` + envAPIBaseURL + `, --token / ` + envAPIToken + `.`,
72			Args: cobra.NoArgs,
73			RunE: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {
74				// `--json` is a promise that this invocation answers in JSON. The
75				// group node has no result of its own, and printing human help to
76				// stdout under exit 0 told a machine caller "here is your JSON" and
77				// handed it prose instead. It must not quietly run `list` either:
78				// that verb is HOSTED, and turning an inert invocation into network
79				// egress is exactly what the opt-in gates above exist to prevent.
